From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:10:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xl: look for the UEFI of the device being run

firmware() looked for redwood's SILICIUM_UEFI.fd only, so any other
device with a UEFI build (davinci) was sent through U-Boot. Look under
$DEVICE, which the Makefile exports, with redwood still the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xl b/xl
index 490ed44..0342b9a 100755
--- a/xl
+++ b/xl
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ firmware() {
 	case "${XL_FIRMWARE:-}" in
 	u-boot|silicium) echo "$XL_FIRMWARE"; return ;;
 	esac
-	if [ -f Mu-Silicium/Build/redwoodPkg/RELEASE_CLANGPDB/FV/SILICIUM_UEFI.fd ] || [ -f devices/redwood/prebuilt/SILICIUM_UEFI.fd ]; then
+	if [ -f Mu-Silicium/Build/${DEVICE:-redwood}Pkg/RELEASE_CLANGPDB/FV/SILICIUM_UEFI.fd ] || [ -f devices/${DEVICE:-redwood}/prebuilt/SILICIUM_UEFI.fd ]; then
 		echo silicium
 	else
 		echo u-boot
